  "id": "appraisal-theory",
  "term": "appraisal theory",
  "definition": "Appraisal theory is a way of understanding emotion as a dynamic process that can be interpreted through appraisal models, such as the Component Process Model. In this view, changes in emotion over time can be linked to patterns in other responses, including physiological activity.",
